data.content:
Output is `{"name":"Jane","age":30}` as expected. Here's the full program:

```csharp
using System.Text.Json;

var options = new JsonSerializerOptions { PropertyNamingPolicy = JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase };
var json = JsonSerializer.Serialize(new Person("Jane", 30), options);
Console.WriteLine(json);

public record Person(string Name, int Age);
```

The key piece is `JsonNamingPolicy.CamelCase` — set it on `JsonSerializerOptions.PropertyNamingPolicy` and all PascalCase properties (`Name`, `Age`) are serialized as camelCase (`name`, `age`).
